.\logs\codex-20261027T2136388310238Z-ed956557521e4ee68b5c6d7e5658cc7f.log:261:docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:136:Offline validation uses temporary records, fake clocks/connections, and guarded credential/database interfaces; it includes concurrency, negative paths, durable/exclusive writes, denial persistence, expiry/retention, artifact/prerequisite separation, direct/Alembic bypass checks, acknowledged and uncertain commit outcomes, and recovery blocking. Deterministic autonomy review finds no AI in ordinary authorization, expiry, audit, execution, or recovery decisions. Owner review, issuance, and reconciliation remain explicit administrative controls. Offline tests do not establish live operational or production readiness; independent artifact review and a later separately authorized testing-only baseline validation are still required.
.\logs\codex-20261027T2136388310238Z-ed956557521e4ee68b5c6d7e5658cc7f.log:267:docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:286:- Next database checkpoint: independent review of exact 0003 artifacts/prerequisites, then a separate owner-authorized **TESTING** `0002_state_requests -> 0003_notifications` validation. Verify real PostgreSQL partial-index races, constraints, dependency/type ACL and column-grant semantics, runtime identity, persistence, rollback/uncertain outcomes and real API/browser behavior. DEVELOPMENT requires successful TESTING evidence for matching artifacts and its own authorization. No live readiness is claimed by offline success.
